.TH start-cli-registry-metrics-installs 1  "installs "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-registry\-metrics\-installs \- Count package installs and updates reported by StartOS, with optional filters
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli registry metrics installs\fR [\fB\-\-pkg\-id\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-after\fR] [\fB\-\-before\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Count package installs and updates reported by StartOS, with optional filters
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-pkg\-id\fR \fI<PKG_ID>\fR
Filter by package ID
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Filter by version
.TP
\fB\-\-after\fR \fI<AFTER>\fR
Start of time range (RFC 3339 timestamp)
.TP
\fB\-\-before\fR \fI<BEFORE>\fR
End of time range (RFC 3339 timestamp)
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR
Also count each day, week (from Monday) or month in the range, in UTC
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
day
.IP \(bu 2
week
.IP \(bu 2
month
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
